(MATTHEW KAPHAN) writes:
>What is the method to keep nymphs from stealing things from me, and 
>lepracauns also?  I just started playing the game, and I'm having a lot
>of trouble staying alive unless i'm in exploratory mode.  Any hints to help
>me out?

The most obvious way to keep nymphs from robbing you blind is to leave
them alone.  If you must kill one, zapping it with a wand of
cancellation will make it unable to steal anything.  My usual tactic
is to leave them alone until I get telepathy and a blindfold, and then
only kill as many as needed.  btw, if you have a ring of adornment,
they will always steal that first.  They will not pay special
attention to a mirror in your inventory, but if you a)pply the mirror
in their direction they will steal it from your inventory (even if
they weren't close enough to touch you).

Leprechauns, in contrast, are much easier to handle.  Simply drop all
of your gold out of its sight, then beat the tar out of it.  It won't
teleport if it can't steal money from you.
 
